=== Extras and special episodes ===
Both episodes nine and ten were masterclasses by Paul and Mary, where they demonstrated how to make the '''Technical Challenges''' that they had set throughout the series. Episode nine showed the first four of the series; Coffee and walnut Battenberg, Tarte au Citron, Focaccia and Brandy Snaps. Episode ten showed the last four of the series; Pork pies, Chocolate roulade, Iced fingers and Sachertorte.
Episode eleven went back and revisited the bakers from series one to catch up with the contestants.

==Post-show career==
Some of the contestants went on to a career in baking or had a change of career after appearing on the show.

[[Joanne Wheatley]] has written two bestselling books on baking, ''A Passion for Baking'' published on 16 May 2013,<ref name="metro"/> and ''Home Baking'' initially as a [[Sainsbury's]] exclusive.  She writes a monthly column for ''Sainsbury's'' magazine and is a regular guest columnist for ''[[The Sun (United Kingdom)|The Sun]]'' newspaper.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.sainsburysentertainment.co.uk/en/Books/Hardback/Jo-Wheatley/Home-Baking-Sainsbury-s-Exclusive/product.html?product=E11217799 |title=Home Baking [Sainsbury's Exclusive] |work=Sainsbury |url-status=dead |archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20130905100223/http://www.sainsburysentertainment.co.uk/en/Books/Hardback/Jo-Wheatley/Home-Baking-Sainsbury-s-Exclusive/product.html?product=E11217799 |archivedate=5 September 2013 }}</ref><ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.exacteditions.com/read/sainsburysmagazine/february-2013-34157/5/3 |title=Sainsbury's Magazine – February content |work=Exact Editions Ltd. }}</ref> She runs cookery courses from her home in Essex,<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.josblueaga.com |title=Jo's Blue AGA}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |url=http://mojomums.co.uk/great-british-bake-off-winner-jo-wheatley-interview/ |title=Great British Bake Off Winner Jo Wheatley Interview |work=Mojo Mums }}</ref> and has appeared in various television programmes such as ''[[The Alan Titchmarsh Show]]'' and ''[[What's Cooking? (British TV series)|What's Cooking]]''.<ref>{{cite news |url=https://www.independent.co.uk/arts-entertainment/tv/news/great-british-bake-off-2014-what-past-winners-are-doing-now-from-edd-kimber-to-last-years-frances-quinn-9780390.html |archive-url=https://ghostarchive.org/archive/20220618/https://www.independent.co.uk/arts-entertainment/tv/news/great-british-bake-off-2014-what-past-winners-are-doing-now-from-edd-kimber-to-last-years-frances-quinn-9780390.html |archive-date=18 June 2022 |url-access=subscription |url-status=live |title=Great British Bake Off 2014: What past winners are doing now from Edd Kimber to last year's Frances Quinn |author=Jess Denham |date=7 October 2014 |work=The Independent }}</ref>

Holly Bell teaches baking classes and for a time worked as an occasional radio presenter on BBC Radio Leicester.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.foodheavenmag.com/2012/07/an-interview-with-holly-bell/ |title=An interview with Holly Bell |work=Food Heaven |date=10 July 2012 |url-status=dead |archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20131004224355/http://www.foodheavenmag.com/2012/07/an-interview-with-holly-bell/ |archivedate=4 October 2013 }}</ref> She also appeared as a guest presenter on QVC shopping channel.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.bbcgoodfoodbakesandcakesshow.com/Content/Holly-Bell |title=Holly Bell |work=Good Food Bakes and Cakes Show}}</ref>  She wrote an [[eBook]] called ''Ready, Steady, Bake!'' which was published on 5 July 2012,<ref>{{cite web |url=http://mebookshelfandi.co.uk/2013/04/30/kindle-baking-book-bargain/ |title=Kindle Baking Book Bargain!! |work=Me, Bookshelf and I }}</ref> and published a book ''Recipes from a Normal Mum'' on 17 July 2014.<ref>{{citation |url=https://www.telegraph.co.uk/foodanddrink/10973388/Cookbook-of-the-week-Recipes-from-a-Normal-Mum.html |title=Cookbook of the week: Recipes from a Normal Mum |author= Carolyn Hart |date= 17 July 2014 |work=The Daily Telegraph }}</ref>

Mary-Anne Boermans wrote a book on baking, ''Great British Bakes: Forgotten Treasures for Modern Bakers'', which was published on 7 November 2013.<ref>{{cite news |url=https://www.independent.co.uk/life-style/food-and-drink/features/on-the-menu-lardo-london-stolichnya-salted-karamel-vodka-maryanne-boermans-great-british-bakes-eatplaylove2013-perrier-8732580.html |archive-url=https://ghostarchive.org/archive/20220618/https://www.independent.co.uk/life-style/food-and-drink/features/on-the-menu-lardo-london-stolichnya-salted-karamel-vodka-maryanne-boermans-great-british-bakes-eatplaylove2013-perrier-8732580.html |archive-date=18 June 2022 |url-access=subscription |url-status=live |title=On The Menu: Lardo London; Stolichnya' Salted Karamel vodka; Mary-Anne Boermans' Great British Bakes; EatPlayLove2013; Perrier |author=Samuel Muston |date=25 July 2013 |work= The Independent }}</ref> She later participated in the 2016 rendition of ''The Great Christmas Bake Off'' where she was declared the special's Star Baker.

Janet Basu participated in the 2016 rendition of ''The Great New Year's Bake Off''.

Robert Billington participated in the 2017 rendition of ''The Great New Year's Bake Off''.

